This product includes data from third parties, under their own licenses:

- data/countries.csv: country centres from the Google DSPL canonical
  countries table (https://developers.google.com/public-data/docs/canonical/countries_csv),
  part of the DSPL tools, BSD 3-Clause License, Copyright Google Inc.
  Used for the coarse distances of the account takeover rules.

- data/calling_codes.csv: the international calling code of each country,
  from Google's libphonenumber metadata
  (https://github.com/google/libphonenumber, resources/PhoneNumberMetadata.xml),
  Apache License 2.0, Copyright Google LLC. Used by `calling_code()` and
  `event.phone_code`.

- data/public_suffix_list.dat: the Public Suffix List
  (https://publicsuffix.org/list/public_suffix_list.dat), Mozilla Public
  License 2.0 (https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/), maintained by the Public
  Suffix List project. Used unmodified for `event.email_registered_domain`.

Lists that openfraud can download (only with `[server] fetch_lists = true`)
are NOT part of this repository and keep their own licenses:

- disposable-email-domains (https://github.com/disposable/disposable-email-domains),
  MIT License.
- IPtoASN (https://iptoasn.com), the network table of `[networks]`, public
  domain (Open Data Commons PDDL).
- The Tor Project's bulk exit list (https://check.torproject.org/torbulkexitlist).
- X4BNet lists_vpn (https://github.com/X4BNet/lists_vpn), data centre and VPN
  ranges, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024 X4B (Mathew Heard).
- FireHOL abusers_1d (https://iplists.firehol.org/?ipset=firehol_abusers_1d),
  the list `abuse_ips`, an aggregate of StopForumSpam, CleanTalk, BotScout
  and other sources, each under its own terms.
